consumer.addRecord(new ConsumerRecord<>(TOPIC, 1, 0, TP1_KEY, TP1_VALUE));
consumer.addRecord(new ConsumerRecord<>(TOPIC, 1, 1, TP1_KEY, TP1_VALUE_NEW));
and achieved by "consumedRecords";
Inside of "ConsumerRecords", in order to turn "records", 
which is a HashMap[TopicPartition, List[ConsumerRecord[K, V]]], 
into Iterator[ConsumerRecord[K, V]];
We can just guarantee the sequence underneath same key, while we cannot assure the sequence under different keys;
Am I wrong?
